public class SelectionSort {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        int[] arr = {5, 8, 2, 7, 1};
        selectionSort(arr);
        for (int num : arr) {
            System.out.print(num + " ");
        }
    }

    public static void selectionSort(int[] arr) {
        int n = arr.length;
        for (int i = 0; i < n - 1; i++) {
            int minIndex = i;
            for (int j = i + 1; j < n; j++) {
                if (arr[j] < arr[minIndex]) {
                    minIndex = j;
                }
            }
            // Swap the found minimum element with the first element
            int temp = arr[minIndex];
            arr[minIndex] = arr[i];
            arr[i] = temp;
        }
    }
}
```

This Java program implements the selection sort algorithm to sort an array of integers. The `selectionSort` method sorts the array in ascending order, and the sorted array is printed out at the end.
